# a single value replaced by a disjunction that does not contain it: the
# prior value is a counterexample (beside widen-single-to-union)
-- old.cue --
t!: "a"
-- new.cue --
t!: "b" | "c"
-- out --
incompatible
t is now "b" | "c", which has no alternative for the prior "a" (rule value-narrowed) @ new.cue:1:1
